  data: {
    LLM: "Don't think, just play. Scan both piles constantly. If you have a run (5, 6, 7), arrange them in your hand so you can slam them down in one motion.\n\nBlocking: If you see your opponent hesitating with a card, play on that pile to change the number and mess them up. If you have doubles (two 6s), play one on a 5, wait for opponent to play 7? No, play 6 on 5, then play 7 on 6? Speed is key.\n\nMemory: Use your peripheral vision to see what the opponent is holding if they are sloppy. If they have mostly high cards, play low cards to keep the piles in low numbers.",
    Player: "Don't think, just play. Scan both piles constantly. If you have a run (5, 6, 7), arrange them in your hand so you can slam them down in one motion.\n\nBlocking: If you see your opponent hesitating with a card, play on that pile to change the number and mess them up. If you have doubles (two 6s), play one on a 5, wait for opponent to play 7? No, play 6 on 5, then play 7 on 6? Speed is key.\n\nMemory: Use your peripheral vision to see what the opponent is holding if they are sloppy. If they have mostly high cards, play low cards to keep the piles in low numbers.",
